==Battleground==
*3 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*1 [[Gory Dark]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
**6 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
**2 [[Shy Boy]]s spawn, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Doge Darks, Gory Darks, Shy Boys and even Dark Emperor Nyandam appear in this stage, which is a lot harder than [[4th Round: Dawn (Veteran)]]. To deal with the Gory Darks, [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] or [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl Cat]] are highly recommended to stop their pushing. The Doge Darks are weaker, so Paris Cat and Ring Girl Cat work against them just fine. For the Shy Boys, [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] or [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Valkyrie Cat]] are recommended. Bahamut Cat can one shot the Shy Boys at a high enough level, and Valkyrie Cat's damage adds up overtime when she is protected well enough. For Dark Emperor Nyandam, use a similar strategy to EoC Chapter 2 Moon, using the [[Cat Cannon]] to interrupt his attacks whenever possible.

